cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "tensor-rank-toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A C++20 research library for exact tensor and bilinear rank over finite fields
  and over the rationals, built on Givaro: a descent heuristic, a complete
  exhaustive search, the same tree cut by what has been built rather than by a
  target, quotienting by symmetry, SAT and SMT encodings of the rank
  question with DRAT proof checking, operator sparsification down to the provable
  minimum over every change of basis, and upper bounds
  read off an algebraic curve, with a CUDA leaf scan measured against the host
  path it would replace. Every count is computed in exact arithmetic and nothing
  is ever a float, because a search over ranks and over counts of nonzeros gives
  a different answer when it is nearly right.
type: software
version: 0.4.1
date-released: "2026-08-23"
